      "type": "text",
      "text": "I've marked the run as UNKNOWN and asked for a human. The pressure gauge the growth stage requires isn't installed, so tube pressure can't be checked, though every installed sensor looks normal. There's no characterization yet, so there's no evidence either way on whether the material grew.\n\n- **Temperature:** It's holding at 750.0 °C against a 750 °C setpoint. The ramp tracked the setpoint closely, and a brief overshoot to 760 °C at the start of growth settled.\n- **Heater power and argon flow:** Heater power is steady at about 45%, and argon is at 99.6 sccm against a 100 sccm setpoint.\n- **Exhaust oxygen:** Purge brought it down from about 28,800 ppm to single digits, and it has stayed at 3–8 ppm since. That argues against a leak letting air in.\n- **What can't be seen:** A problem that mainly shows up as a change in pressure, such as a blocked exhaust, would be invisible with these sensors.\n\nTo settle it, someone needs to confirm tube pressure, either with a gauge or a manual check. The sample also needs characterizing after the run."
     }
